  "notes": "\"Simple isn't easy\": the parameters here are mostly subtractions, and silence is authored as a device rather than as an absence. The kick runs 1–3 hits a bar, the hats are `continuous: false`, `melody.emptyBarBias` is 0.35, and the drop is the 808 arriving rather than layers being added — hence one enormous `heavy`-distortion 808 in the lowest register on this bench with a long `portamentoMs`. Snare rolls and reverse crashes are the primary event markers, so `snareRoll.buildAndStopProb` is 0.55 and `dualLayerProb` 0.35, with `reverse`, `crash` and `impact` on the perc lanes. The arrangement block is authored rather than inherited because the research makes it a parameter: long intros with delayed drops and a full drop-out before each one. ⚠ `hihat.fillDensity` is 0.32 rather than lower — the hats are sparse by description, but a model that declares a hat block owes every seed a hat, and below ~0.28 some seeds produce a bar with none. ⚠ INFERRED: the two-chord families. The research says \"a single drone or two-chord bed\"; which two chords is not sourced. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
